<title>USA: Nematron says it topped Q1 forecasts.</title>
<headline>Nematron says it topped Q1 forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>ANN ARBOR, Mich. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nematron Corp on Wednesday said its December 31 first-quarter earnings of $11,000 were consistent with the company's plan and exceeded prevailing analyst expectations of a loss of $194,000, or $0.04 a share.</p>
<p>The manufacturer of industrial automation products also said it expected to release its OpenControl software for factory automation and machine control late in the second quarter.</p>
<p>It said it would follow that with the introduction of other software and hardware products later in the year.</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
